e land is woods. In the woods a grass tile stands a Tree (World of Daggerfall's Tree records for the climate's summer archive) at 0.5 and undergrowth at 0.12; on the plains a lone Tree at 0.02 and bushes, flowers and rocks at 0.1; dirt takes 0.6 of those, stone 0.15. Each flat stands inside its own tile (0.1-0.9 of it each way, on the ground there by `groundAt`), never on a corner, never on the road tile beside it, never on a track the road painter laid (its `paths` mask - a track over dirt leaves the record dirt). Every tile draws its own dice off its WORLD tile (`tileDraw`, murmur3's finaliser), so a place one peer stands and another does not moves only the flats about it. The woods close round a dungeon, keep, shrine, ruin, graveyard or coven (LocationTypes 4, 7, 9, 10, 12, 13) and every World of Daggerfall SITE (each pick's own footprint - its rect and every object of it grown by the site margin, `wodSiteFootprint`; never its rock fields and mountains, `wodPiecewise`, 93% of the mod's instances, which are scenery), and draw back from every other place into fields; full inside 10 tiles (6 for a town), none past 30 (26), faded out over the 12 tiles before the pixel's edge so no forest is cut off by one. Every place's footprint, widened by DFU's clearance 4, is a clearing - tested whole (NT2's quirk is DFU's scatter's). A wood's flats keep out of the rock pieces (`insideRocks`), and the day's Oblivion Gate keeps its clearing of nature in both modes (`pointNearGate`, as of World of Daggerfall's flats). Under Real forests a Tree flat carries how wooded its tile is, and Logging's trees of the day stand at the woods' own (`FOREST.woods`, 0.5) wherever a pixel has any. KEPT: DFU's tests on the tile (steepness 50 - asked of the gradient itself, no arctangent in the decision - the beach line, tiles 1-3 only), the answer's shape (plus `wood`). Deserts (DFU's Desert base type: the Desert and Subtropical climates) and an archive with no Tree table stand DFU's scatter byte for byte, as does the switch off. COST, measured on the real WOODS.WLD over 675 land pixels (2026-10-01): flats 1,856 a pixel against DFU's 1,900; Trees 1,274 against 530 (2.4x - DFU's elevation scale is not applied, a lowland wood is a wood), at most 7,664 against 2,296; the layout 1.66 ms a pixel against 1.31 (the lattice). The far rings draw every Tree (`world/flatDistance.js`), so a wooded horizon costs more than DFU's - the Features row is the dial. AUDIT FOREST1 (a second lens over the branch, read-only, then paid): F1 rock fields and mountains had become hidden places; F2 the cost was understated; F3 the patch notes said Logging's trees stood in the woods and 55% stood on the plains; F4 eight survivors; F5 the gate's clearing kept no nature; F6 a stream of dice cascaded a place's difference across a pixel, and the kill door split a room; F7 camps reached past their clearing; F8 trees stood on tracks over dirt - all paid as above. Verified on the real game data (`tools/grassLookProbe.mjs`). `test/forest1.test.js` (16), `tools/mutants/forest1.json` (27 mutants, all dead). | the owner, 2026-10-01 (handed the thread) |
