+| mods1_api.test.js | 19 | MODS1 (2026-10-13, a player: the accessibility mod "needs to be a module like a rust crate type of mod ... unchained from versioning ... it should work online" - `06-Systems/Mod-API.md`) - THE MOD API (`src/mods/modApi.js`, `moduleHost.js`, `modBus.js`, `keysPanel.js`; `app/lib/moduleFiles.cjs`; `src/ui/modulesCard.js`). The modules themselves (Beardd's Wayfarer) are tested in their own repository. A MANIFEST: read with its defaults (entry `module.js`), unknown fields, a bad slug, version, api, events, a path for an entry and a bad sha256 refused with their reasons. UNCHAINED FROM THE GAME: a module names an interface, never a build; one for interface N runs on N or more; it cannot reach past its own api; a field naming a game build is refused. THE EVENT TABLE IS APPEND-ONLY: every event, its interface and its arguments in order, pinned. THE BUS: a module hears the events its manifest lists and no others, a failing listener is isolated and named once, a module that keeps failing is switched off, a switched-off module hears nothing. A MODULE'S HANDLE: its own settings apart from every other's, its line and key only while it is on, exactly the handle's keys and frozen, nothing of the net in the source. WORDS IN THE PLAYER'S LANGUAGE: a module's dfo.t reads the game's own table (the player's language), its English where the table has no row, a host with no text core or a failing one the English. THE HOST: each module judged and started on its own (running, off, refused for a future interface, a wrong folder, a bad manifest, a missing file, a hash mismatch, no default export, a throw); a module that is off is never imported; no shell, no modules; a duplicate id refused. THE PLAYER'S SWITCHES: the ids turned off, kept, a junk record none. THE SHELL'S DOOR over a real temp folder: slug folders only, plain `.js` names, nothing past them. THE SEAMS by source: the HUD, the shared magic engine and the quest bridge announce their events on the one b